# Netlify redirects.
#
# SPA catch-all. react-router owns the URL, but the server sees a real request
# for a real path on a hard load or a deep link — /lab, or /specimen/TBA-0042
# later. Without this, Netlify looks for a file at that path, finds none, and
# returns its 404 page instead of the app.
#
# The 200 is the important part: it rewrites rather than redirects, so the
# browser keeps the requested URL and react-router resolves the route from it.
# A 301/302 here would bounce every deep link to the home page.
#
# Last rule, and deliberately last: Netlify applies the first match, so any
# future proxy or redirect must go above this line.
/*  /index.html  200
